                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Simple and cute tile breaking puzzle game where you have to plan your route moving shapes to their matching keyholes to unlock the level exit. You cannot traverse a tile more than once as the floor will fall away but you also don’t have to break every tile to complete the level.\n\nThere are 100 levels + bonus Christmas levels. They are untimed, have an undo button, as well as a generous hint system without ‘hand holding’. You also cannot fall off the edge. I found the controls a bit loose and floaty, occasionally overshot and cornered myself into an unwinnable situation.\n\nLater on more mechanics are added on top of the basic gameplay, for example -  buttons, tile skipping, portals, and ‘ ice hockey’. The difficulty progression feels right for a casual game, never too much but still enough of a challenge.\n",
